# SPEC: 49_static_analysis,49_static_off
# Does `sys.exit` really end the program — and with THIS return value?
#
# The whole corpus depends on it: every FAIL branch ends this way.  Until 2026-10-15
# it said `- exit: [1]` there, a key the compiler silently discarded
# (spec/49 §2a).  The branches ran through, returned 0, and the suite reported
# PASS for tests that printed "FAIL".  This test is the guard against that.
#
# Expected exit code: 3
- print: ["sys.exit is called now"]
- call: [sys.exit, 3]
- print: ["FAIL this line must never appear"]
